  "modified": "2026-08-05T05:14:33Z",
  "summary": "Heavily obfuscated CLI package with mailer / sender / verifier modules",
  "details": "monogrok 1.0.1 ships ~49 JavaScript files where every source file (commands, utilities, helpers, models, mailer backends) is heavily obfuscated using hex-identifier renaming (`_0x4e678b`-style symbols on line 1 of each file). The package's directory layout suggests bulk-mail / SMTP tooling: `functions/sender/mailers/` contains backends for EWS, Zimbra, free-mail, MX, proxy, and local mailers; `functions/verifier/`, `functions/extractor/`, `functions/sorter/`, `functions/ip-rotate/`, `functions/redirect/`, and `commands/auth.js` / `commands/send.js` / `commands/verify.js` are similarly obfuscated. Pervasive obfuscation across an entire CLI codebase (rather than a single minified vendor bundle) is uncommon for legitimate open-source tooling and is consistent with either commercial-IP protection of a paid CLI or with mass-mail / credential-verification abuseware. The behavioral semantics of the obfuscated code were not fully traced in this run, so the specific network destinations, credential handling, and any install/import-time side effects are not verified here. Disposition is human review: the obfuscation + mailer/verifier/extractor surface area combination warrants manual de-obfuscation before installer trust is granted.",
